Name: zune-jpeg
URL: https://crates.io/crates/zune-jpeg
Version: 0.5.16-rc2
Revision: c93e77f5652f76fa77bf7a3823f360f65ceaab6f
Update Mechanism: Manual (https://crbug.com/449898466)
License: Apache-2.0
License File: //third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/zune-jpeg-v0_5/LICENSE-APACHE
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: yes

Description: A fast, correct and safe jpeg decoder

Local Modifications:
- Keep the age-eligible 0.5.16-rc2 package as the download base. Chromium's
  minimum publish-age policy currently excludes 0.5.16-rc3.
- Backport the accepted upstream prerequisites at
  2f9086b07cdf5a36621ce18f79d310f99b751de9, including merged raw/scanline and
  YCCK-to-CMYK support. Preserve the existing PR443 fix and its attribution.
- Apply provenance-labelled, non-duplicated Rust-source deltas from:
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/487
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/494
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/499
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/498
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/504
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/506
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/508
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/505
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/507
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/525
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/526
  Each patch records its published PR head and source-stage provenance.
  PR498 includes its eighth-step extension; subsequent patches are rebased
  onto that revision rather than carrying a second patch for the same PR.
- The source through patch 0010 is byte-identical to the validated combination
  of PR487 through PR507. Keep coded/raw geometry, strict errors, growing
  input and full-frame recovery separate from buffered publication bounds.
  Reduced output supports every n/8 ratio for n from 1 through 7 and is
  frame-buffered. Include PR498's eighth-step extension at
  50e283a32a465cdeaa0d235e0187791b227f6e21; the cumulative source matches
  8f3ad58e9a7dc6bca100cf276ecc11324e339cef.
- Patch 0011 backports PR525 at
  5dbe923c726ded1405960ecf5ed924034b8412cf, including configured row dispatch.
  Patch 0012 backports PR526 at
  b5ad1d9cffac891868e9c86b6fe1aa0a56afbcc9 on top of it.
  Both are rebased onto the existing stack rather than replacing it.
  Preserve PR505's single-rounding chroma filter in fused AVX2 upsampling,
  i32 sequential coefficient storage and native recovery behavior. Adapt
  dispatch and marker-state tests to the existing types and state.
  Leave zune-core unchanged. Dispatch tests follow its effective SIMD policy;
  explicit scalar references and no-SIMD builds cover scalar output separately.
- Track upstream acceptance and release availability in:
  https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/issues/503
  Remove maintained patches only after verifying their complete behavior is
  included in the selected upstream release.
